    "voice": {
      "learned": true,
      "tone": "Warm, sensory and quietly aspirational — it sells the ritual of writing by hand, not just the object, favouring gentle emphasis (italics, asterisks) over hard sell.",
      "rhythm": "Short declarative or fragment sentences for impact, interleaved with one longer flowing sentence that does the explaining; paragraphs rarely run past three sentences; em dashes used to add a second beat to a line.",
